<content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<para>Display the following polynomials to students one at a time to allow them to decide the best way to factor each
  polynomial.</para>
<br/>
<table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
  <thead>
    <row>
        <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Polynomials</entry>
</row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        \(27q^2 − 3\)
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        \(x^2 − 10x + 25 − y^2\)
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        \(16x^2 − 72x + 81\)
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        \(36y^2 + 12y + 1\)
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        \(4p^2 − 100\)
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        \(x^2 + 12x + 36 − y^2\)
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
<br/>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<para>Your teacher will display six different polynomials. Sort these polynomials by whether you would factor them using
  the difference of squares or the perfect square trinomial method.</para>
<para>Draw a table similar to this on a sheet of paper. Record your results. If a polynomial requires both methods, place
  it in both columns.</para>
<br/>
<table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Difference of Squares Method</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Perfect Square Trinomial Method</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
         <br/>
         <br/>
         
      </entry>
      <entry>
         <br/>
         <br/>
         
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
<br/>
<para>Write down your answers. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
<para class="os-raise-text-bold">Answer:</para>
<table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Difference of Squares Method</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Perfect Square Trinomial Method</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        \(27q^2 − 3\)<br/>
        \(4p^2 − 100\)<br/>
        \(x^2 − 10x + 25 − y^2\)<br/>
        \(x^2 + 12x + 36 − y^2\)
      </entry>
      <entry>
        \(16x^2 − 72x + 81\)<br/>
        \(36y^2 + 12y + 1\)<br/>
        \(x^2 − 10x + 25 − y^2\)<br/>
        \(x^2 + 12x + 36 − y^2\)
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table></section>
